{"slug":"ICT","companyName":"Integrated Control Technology (ICT)","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28T02:22:11Z","followerCount":28602,"bio":"Integrated Control Technology (ICT) is a world leading manufacturer of unified electronic access control and security solutions enabling a scalable solution for organizations to protect their people, operations and information.\n\nICT's Protege\u00ae seamlessly integrates a full suite of security management functions and technologies using an open architecture design. offering electronic access control, ID credential issuance and management; alarm monitoring, apartment management, digital video surveillance and management, real-time digital video content analysis, integration of biometric technologies, intrusion detection and smart card functionality, plus integration with a multitude of third-party systems.\n\nBased in Auckland, New Zealand, ICT has a global presence with offices located in Denver (Colorado USA), Amersham (United Kingdom), and Sydney (Australia) to provide full local sales, support and service to our clients and partners around the world.\n\nTo learn more, visit www.ict.co","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-27","text":"Security is still a people problem. Technology just decides how fast you can respond. That\u2019s the thread running through today\u2019s ASIS Qu\u00e9bec 2026 Symposium, built around ethics, best practices, leadership and technology.\nIf you\u2019re weighing how access control, intrusion detection and building automation can work as one platform instead of three, come find Vincent Lescaut on the show floor today!\n#ASISQuebec #PhysicalSecurity #AccessControl","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"Neil Foster and the team are back on the stand at Skydd, and day two is already off to a busy start!\nA big thank you to everyone who has stopped by so far. It's been great to show you ICT's unified, cyber-compliant platform for access control, intrusion detection and building automation.\nStop by, meet the team and get your live demo on stand A06:51. Tomorrow is the final day, so don't miss out!","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-26","text":"Security in logistics is about people as well as assets.\nAgency staff, contractors and drivers come and go, and each of them needs the right access for the right dates.\nProtege GX can make access depend on a current induction or driver's licence, let only booked trucks through the gate and send the fire warden a muster report when the alarm sounds.\nThere's no limit on users, so peak-season staff don't change the licence, and access control, intrusion detection and building automation sit on one platform.\nWorking on a logistics project?\nICT will be at The Security Event Asia.\nLearn about how we secure sites at Stand 1928, Singapore, 10 to 12 November.\n#TSEAsia #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"When we think high security, we often think of banks.\nTheir brick-and-mortar branches must be capable of protecting both staff and assets in an instant.\nProtege GX secures banks across New Zealand, Asia and Canada.\nA teller can raise a silent duress alarm without anyone noticing, the vault opens only for two authorised people and each branch keeps running when the network drops. You can move a bank off its legacy cards one branch at a time, with access control, intrusion detection and building automation on one platform.\nWorking on a banking project?\nTalk it through at Stand 1928, Singapore, 10 to 12 November.\n#TSEAsia #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"Day 1 at Security Canada Central is in full swing!\nOur team has been busy connecting with integrators from across the province, talking through real projects, complex sites and the challenges they\u2019re working to solve.\nIf you\u2019re at the show, stop by booth 523 to say hi to the team see how Protege GX brings access control, intrusion detection and building automation together on one unified platform, and talk with our team about how ICT can help set your next project up for success.\n#SecurityCanadaCentral #ProtegeGX #AccessControl #SecurityIndustry\nRonald Goolcharan | Dale Sellers | Daniel Miclette | Kolin Lee | Pat Alvaro","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"}]}
