{"slug":"ICT","companyName":"Integrated Control Technology (ICT)","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology","fetchedAt":"2026-10-25T22:18:38Z","followerCount":28577,"bio":"Integrated Control Technology (ICT) is a world leading manufacturer of unified electronic access control and security solutions enabling a scalable solution for organizations to protect their people, operations and information.\n\nICT's Protege\u00ae seamlessly integrates a full suite of security management functions and technologies using an open architecture design. offering electronic access control, ID credential issuance and management; alarm monitoring, apartment management, digital video surveillance and management, real-time digital video content analysis, integration of biometric technologies, intrusion detection and smart card functionality, plus integration with a multitude of third-party systems.\n\nBased in Auckland, New Zealand, ICT has a global presence with offices located in Denver (Colorado USA), Amersham (United Kingdom), and Sydney (Australia) to provide full local sales, support and service to our clients and partners around the world.\n\nTo learn more, visit www.ict.co","recentPosts":[{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"Neil Foster and the team are back on the stand at Skydd, and day two is already off to a busy start!\nA big thank you to everyone who has stopped by so far. It's been great to show you ICT's unified, cyber-compliant platform for access control, intrusion detection and building automation.\nStop by, meet the team and get your live demo on stand A06:51. Tomorrow is the final day, so don't miss out!","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"Day one at Skydd is underway!\nNeil Foster, our Regional Sales Director for Northern Europe, is on stand A06:51, joined by Sally Waugh and Connor Banfield.\nVisit the team for a live demonstration of ICT's unified security solution, including biometrics, intercom and CCTV integration.\nWe look forward to seeing you!\n\ud83d\udccd Stand A06:51\n\ud83d\udcc5 20\u201322 October","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"We're exhibiting at The Security Event Asia in Singapore next month, and we're looking forward to catching up with integrators and consultants from across the region.\nYou'll find Ben Italiano and Jacky Chow on Stand 1928 at the Sands Expo & Convention Centre from 10 to 12 November, along with demonstrations in how ICT Protege GX secures sites across the banking, logistics and technology sectors.\n#TSEAsia #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-20","text":"This week, we\u2019re heading to Security Canada Central and we want to hear about your toughest sites.\nMore doors. More users. More systems. More moving parts that all need to work together.\nComplex sites don\u2019t need more complexity. With Protege GX, access control, intrusion detection and building automation come together on one unified platform, with integrations to the video, intercom and business systems your customers already rely on.\nThe result? Fewer systems to manage, less complexity and a solution built to scale with your customers.\n\ud83d\udccd Find the ICT team at Booth 523\n\ud83d\udcc5 October 21\u201322\nBring us your toughest security challenge. We\u2019d love to talk through how Protege GX can simplify it.\n#ICT #SecurityCanadaCentral #AcccessControl #ProtegeGX","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"},{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"When we think high security, we often think of banks.\nTheir brick-and-mortar branches must be capable of protecting both staff and assets in an instant.\nProtege GX secures banks across New Zealand, Asia and Canada.\nA teller can raise a silent duress alarm without anyone noticing, the vault opens only for two authorised people and each branch keeps running when the network drops. You can move a bank off its legacy cards one branch at a time, with access control, intrusion detection and building automation on one platform.\nWorking on a banking project?\nTalk it through at Stand 1928, Singapore, 10 to 12 November.\n#TSEAsia #ICT","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/integrated-control-technology/home/"}]}
